<title>ITALY: Air cargo down 12.95 pct at Tuscany airport in 96.</title>
<headline>Air cargo down 12.95 pct at Tuscany airport in 96.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tuscany's Galileo Galillei airport handled just over eight million kg of cargo in 1996, down 12.95 percent on the 1995 total, said its management company SAT.</p>
<p>But the volume of mail handled was up 17.4 percent to 666,249 kg in 1996, it added.</p>
<p>SAT said it is now examining a plan to attract more cargo currently transported on the ground to instead use flights to and from Galileo Galillei but gave no details.</p>
<p>-Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 8982 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
